# Where `forward` stays a function of its own, its rest parameter arrives as an array that the caller made. `add(...values)` reads the variable `add` and leaves through the stub that calls with a list of arguments,
# as a tail call: the elements are not read here, and the known callee is not called directly.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="forward" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[callee]] = Patchpoint({{*}}Reads:{{*}}ModuleVariables{{*}}:GetModuleVariable)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[values]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK: Patchpoint(b@[[values]]:Register({{*}}), b@[[callee]]:Register({{*}}), $10(b@{{*}}):Register({{*}}), runsWithoutFrame, resultConstraints = WarmAny, Terminal|ExitsSideways
# CHECK-NOT: BB#
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
